---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { facts, stated } from '../data/carriers'

const supply = [
  {
    k: 'Whether it is correlated',
    v: 'the same failure pattern, tested across many deployments, so you can see whether a hit here means a hit everywhere',
  },
  {
    k: 'What actually failed',
    v: 'which control gave way under attack, rather than which controls the insured reported having',
  },
  {
    k: 'What got reached',
    v: 'the boundary that was crossed and what sat behind it, including whether it was a boundary between customers',
  },
  {
    k: 'Whether it moved',
    v: 'the same system re-tested after each deployment, so posture is a series rather than a submission-day snapshot',
  },
]
---

<Base
  title="For carriers and MGAs · Bastion"
  description="Carriers are filing to exclude AI risk because they cannot tell whether one failure is one loss or ten thousand. We generate the evidence that answers that."
>
  <section class="top">
    <div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="page">
      <p class="label">For carriers, MGAs and reinsurers</p>
      <h1>The exclusions are already being filed</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        AIG, Great American and WR Berkley have all gone to regulators for AI
        exclusions. The Berkley language reaches any actual or alleged use of
        AI, including products that merely incorporate it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section sourced">
    <div class="page">
      <p class="label">On the record</p>
      <ul class="facts">
        {
          facts.map((f) => (
            <li>
              <p>{f.claim}</p>
              <a href={f.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                {f.source} ↗
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <p class="label">The stated reason is not what you would expect</p>
      <blockquote>{stated}</blockquote>
      <p class="lede after">
        The blocker carriers describe is correlation, not severity. A single bad
        deployment is underwritable. What cannot be underwritten is not knowing
        whether the failure inside one insured is sitting inside every other
        insured running the same pattern.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section relief">
    <div class="page">
      <h2 class="big">
        That is a question about failure patterns, which is the thing we collect
      </h2>
      <p class="lede">
        We attack live AI systems on purpose and record what broke, across many
        deployments, independent of the insured. It produces the evidence an
        underwriter would need to tell a one-off from a systemic exposure.
      </p>

      <dl class="supply">
        {
          supply.map((s) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{s.k}</dt>
              <dd>{s.v}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page close">
      <div>
        <h2>Worth a conversation before the exclusion becomes the default</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          We are not underwriters and we do not price risk. We generate and
          structure the failure evidence that pricing it would require.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Talk to us about the data</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .top {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem) clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .glow {
    position: absolute;
    inset: -40% -20% auto -20%;
    height: 190%;
    z-index: -1;
    background:
      radial-gradient(42% 44% at 74% 0%, rgba(255, 240, 206, 0.32) 0%, rgba(16, 15, 13, 0) 68%),
      radial-gradient(60% 50% at 84% 6%, rgba(214, 150, 66, 0.18) 0%, rgba(16, 15, 13, 0) 64%);
    filter: blur(24px);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.25rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
    margin-block: 1.1rem 1.35rem;
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .sourced {
    background: var(--panel);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--stone-line);
  }

  .facts {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2.25rem);
  }

  .facts li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--stone-line);
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
  }

  .facts p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .facts a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .facts a:hover {
    color: var(--gold-text);
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gold);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 1rem + 1vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 34ch;
  }

  .after {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .big {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 1.15rem + 1.9vw, 2.5rem);
    max-width: 26ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.3rem;
  }

  .supply {
    margin: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    padding-top: 1.6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--stone-line);
  }

  dt {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .close {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.75rem 2.5rem;
  }

  .close h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 1.1rem + 1.3vw, 2.1rem);
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .facts,
    .supply,
    .close {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
